Dear Dr. Voss,

I am writing to seek your advice regarding a patient who requires urgent
hepatology review. Marcus Ellery (MRN-47892, age 47) has returned
markedly abnormal liver function tests on his 2026 annual checkup:

  ALT: 187 U/L
  AST: 124 U/L

The abdominal ultrasound on the same date showed mild hepatic steatosis
without focal lesion. No biliary duct dilatation. No hepatic mass.

Could you advise on the most appropriate workup sequence before referral?
I understand your hepatology clinic requires pre-authorisation from the
patient's health insurer — I am awaiting their response.

Best regards,
Dr. Priya Nambiar
Merton Health Clinic

